# CODEOWNERS — per-feature-module ownership
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Goal: as the backend migrates from technical-layer-first (routes/, services/)
# to feature modules (src/modules/<domain>/), each module gets an owning team so
# reviews route to the right people and parallel teams stop colliding on shared
# files. One module per line; later globs win, so list the most specific last.
#
# ALL LINES ARE COMMENTED until real GitHub handles/teams are filled in. A
# CODEOWNERS entry with an unknown owner makes GitHub warn on every PR, so do not
# uncomment a line until its @team / @user exists in this org.
#
# Pilot (feature-module migration): the inventory module has been extracted to
# artifacts/api-server/src/modules/inventory/. Uncomment + set the owner when a
# team handle exists:
#
# /artifacts/api-server/src/modules/inventory/   @medicore/REPLACE-ME
#
# Planned modules (migrate one per PR; clinical last):
# /artifacts/api-server/src/modules/identity/    @medicore/REPLACE-ME
# /artifacts/api-server/src/modules/billing/     @medicore/REPLACE-ME
# /artifacts/api-server/src/modules/imaging/     @medicore/REPLACE-ME
# /artifacts/api-server/src/modules/reporting/   @medicore/REPLACE-ME
# /artifacts/api-server/src/modules/clinical/    @medicore/REPLACE-ME
#
# Platform kernel (policy/audit/RLS/encryption/runtime) is cross-cutting — keep a
# single owning team; do NOT split it across feature modules:
# /artifacts/api-server/src/platform/            @medicore/REPLACE-ME
